# %%TITLE%% (`%%NAME%%`)

Generated by `php artisan make:module %%NAME%%`. Developer docs: `docs/modules.md` and `docs/publishing-and-preview.md` in the CodeArt repository.

## What is here
- `module.json`: the manifest (permissions: %%PERMISSIONS_JSON%%).
- `src/Models/%%MODEL%%.php`: the translatable model%%WORKFLOW_TEXT%%.
- `src/Http/%%STUDLY%%Controller.php`, `routes/web.php`: admin screens (thin; the logic is in core).
- `src/%%STUDLY%%Table.php`: the list. `src/%%MODEL%%Policy.php`: who may do what.
%%if widget%%
- `src/%%STUDLY%%Widget.php`: the dashboard widget (real counts only).
%%endif%%
- `resources/lang/{sr,en}/module.php`: texts; `sr-Cyrl` is generated (`php artisan lang:transliterate --path=resources/lang`).
- `config/%%NAME%%.php`: `public_url`, the address of the real public page, used by the preview.
- `tests/`: Pest tests that run without edits.

## Where to customize
- Fields: `formFields()` and `translatedAttributes()` in the model, the rules in the controller, a migration for new columns.
- Look of the admin form: publish the views or edit `resources/views/form.blade.php`.
- Who gets which permission by default: the `GrantModulePermissions` call in the service provider.

## Checks
In the monorepo `make:module` links `vendor` to core's (git ignores it); then, inside this folder: `vendor/bin/pest`, `vendor/bin/pint --test`, `vendor/bin/phpstan analyse`. Tests need the MariaDB test database (`DB_DATABASE`, default `test`).

## Public site
```blade
@php($page = \Codeart\Core\Publishing\Preview::model(request(), \%%NS%%\Models\%%MODEL%%::class) ?? \%%NS%%\Models\%%MODEL%%::published()->%%LOOKUP%%->firstOrFail())
@php($content = \Codeart\Core\Publishing\Preview::resolve(request(), $page))
<h1>{{ $content->%%TITLE_FIELD%% }}</h1>
```
